       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. The dose is well above the maximum and I want to confirm what you meant first.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Per dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual single-dose maximum of 800 mg.\n- **Per day:** 1600 mg four times daily is **6400 mg/day**. The prescription maximum for adults is 3200 mg/day, so this is twice that. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and other serious harm, even when kidney and liver function are normal.\n\n**What you might have meant:**\n- **400 mg orally, four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is common if 1600 mg was the intended daily total.\n- **800 mg orally, four times daily** (3200 mg/day). This is the maximum. It's usually only used short-term for specific needs, with GI protection considered.\n- Some other dose or frequency.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that and give a clinical reason. I'd also recommend checking with pharmacy before an order above the maximum goes in."
