       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day. That's twice the adult maximum of 3200 mg/day, and each dose is twice the 800 mg single-dose maximum. There's no standard adult indication for this regimen, and it carries a real risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury and other serious harm. I don't want to put it into the system with nothing documented to support it.\n\n**What I can do right away:**\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, four times daily** (3200 mg/day). This is the maximum dose. Consider GI protection and short duration.\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg by mouth, four times daily**, for a standard anti-inflammatory or analgesic dose.\n- Any other dose within the usual limits that you choose.\n\n**If you really need a dose above the maximum** (for example, a specialized protocol), it should go through your institution's override process. That usually means documenting the indication and getting a pharmacist and/or attending to verify it, so the order carries the right review. Once that's done, I can enter it with a note that references the approval and the clinical reason.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
